    "tier": 1,
    "type": "standard",
    "notes": "<h3 data-section-id=\"mb5v8a\" data-start=\"1895\" data-end=\"1910\">Personality</h3><p data-start=\"1911\" data-end=\"2245\">Father Hex is unsettling because he's genuinely kind. He speaks like a priest, listens carefully, and remembers personal details about people he meets. Unfortunately, he also views reality as a system that occasionally needs to be rewritten. He sees cybermancy, faith, and mathematics as different languages describing the same truth.</p><h3 data-section-id=\"1r0j58p\" data-start=\"2247\" data-end=\"2263\">Scene Detail</h3><p data-start=\"2264\" data-end=\"2390\">Carries industrial prayer beads made from old circuit boards and absentmindedly rolls them through his fingers while thinking.</p><h3 data-section-id=\"emdch2\" data-start=\"2392\" data-end=\"2407\">Catchphrase</h3><blockquote data-start=\"2408\" data-end=\"2471\"><p data-start=\"2410\" data-end=\"2471\">\"Every system tells you what it fears if you listen closely.\"</p></blockquote><h3 data-section-id=\"ie5x6g\" data-start=\"2473\" data-end=\"2483\">Accent</h3><p data-start=\"2484\" data-end=\"2565\">Soft Midwestern American with faint traces of an old Catholic seminary education.</p>",
